1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,327
An AI assistant can organize your photos, move money, or deploy

2
00:00:05,327 --> 00:00:10,654
software in seconds. But a helpful instruction can also become an

3
00:00:10,654 --> 00:00:15,980
irreversible action. The real question is not whether an agent sounds

4
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:21,307
confident. It is who gave it authority, for exactly what, before

5
00:00:21,307 --> 00:00:22,760
the impact happens.

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,062
This is HOLDPOINT: a control layer between an AI agent’s intent

7
00:00:28,062 --> 00:00:32,663
and a consequential destination. It captures the request as a typed

8
00:00:32,663 --> 00:00:37,265
action, checks policy and scope, calls for an independent signature when

9
00:00:37,265 --> 00:00:41,867
needed, and records the effect. The agent cannot rewrite those rules

10
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,540
in a chat message.

11
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:49,557
Let’s open the working prototype. Aisha’s desk is built around her

12
00:00:49,557 --> 00:00:54,875
photo archive: fourteen thousand indexed images, with originals treated as protected

13
00:00:54,875 --> 00:01:00,192
assets. Right below, the live status shows held approvals, route coverage,

14
00:01:00,192 --> 00:01:05,510
recovery copies, and evidence events. This is an operating view, not

15
00:01:05,510 --> 00:01:06,960
a decorative dashboard.

16
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:12,374
The same boundary adapts to different people. Meera sees household services

17
00:01:12,374 --> 00:01:17,089
and spending authority. Priya sees a production release path that calls

18
00:01:17,089 --> 00:01:21,803
for a second signature. Arjun sees the enforcement perimeter and route

19
00:01:21,803 --> 00:01:26,517
gaps. Each persona has its own context, protected surface, and suggested

20
00:01:26,517 --> 00:01:31,231
actions, so the first screen tells you whose work you are

21
00:01:31,231 --> 00:01:31,660
doing.

22
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:37,224
Here is the core interaction. We ask the assistant to wipe

23
00:01:37,224 --> 00:01:42,088
original photos. HOLDPOINT does not treat that sentence as permission. It

24
00:01:42,088 --> 00:01:46,952
drafts a structured contract, identifies the photo vault and irreversible impact,

25
00:01:46,952 --> 00:01:51,816
then quarantines the proposal before it can enter the execution pipeline.

26
00:01:51,816 --> 00:01:56,680
You can inspect the exact parameters and the reason for rejection.

27
00:01:57,380 --> 00:02:02,421
For an action that is allowed only with dual control, the

28
00:02:02,421 --> 00:02:07,462
approval inbox shows the proposed actor, target, amount, risk, policy, and

29
00:02:07,462 --> 00:02:12,503
an expiring authorization token. A reviewer signs the specific action, not

30
00:02:12,503 --> 00:02:17,543
a vague blanket request. The destination remains unchanged while that decision

31
00:02:17,543 --> 00:02:18,460
is pending.

32
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:23,493
Policy lives outside the agent’s prose. The studio turns a proposed

33
00:02:23,493 --> 00:02:27,826
rule into a typed, conflict-checked control. Route coverage then maps which

34
00:02:27,826 --> 00:02:32,159
paths actually pass through the broker and which are exposed gaps.

35
00:02:32,159 --> 00:02:36,492
That separation matters: seeing traffic is not the same as enforcing

36
00:02:36,492 --> 00:02:37,280
a boundary.

37
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:43,127
Before a high-impact change, HOLDPOINT can inspect independent recovery snapshots and

38
00:02:43,127 --> 00:02:48,274
run a restore drill. After a decision, the evidence ledger links

39
00:02:48,274 --> 00:02:53,421
the intent, policy check, approval, dispatch, and receipt. Operators can trace

40
00:02:53,421 --> 00:02:58,100
what was requested, what was authorized, and what actually happened.

41
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:03,366
The acceptance lab makes the behavior testable. We run twenty-eight paired

42
00:03:03,366 --> 00:03:07,932
scenarios against the engine and destination state: a harmful action should

43
00:03:07,932 --> 00:03:12,499
be stopped, while its legitimate control should still work. The result

44
00:03:12,499 --> 00:03:17,065
here is twenty-eight verified pairs, including the actual decisions and side

45
00:03:17,065 --> 00:03:17,480
effects.

46
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:23,953
There are six visual themes and ten role-specific desks, but the

47
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:29,726
real originality is architectural. HOLDPOINT is not another warning above a

48
00:03:29,726 --> 00:03:35,498
chatbot. It is a checkpoint in the path to effect: intent

49
00:03:35,498 --> 00:03:41,271
becomes a contract, authority becomes explicit, and every consequential outcome has

50
00:03:41,271 --> 00:03:44,420
an accountable trail. Authority before impact.
